WEBVTT

00:02.980 --> 00:04.840
Thank you, Ivy.

00:04.840 --> 00:09.340
We've been able to eradicate the organization 
that has tormented Otolwa for years.

00:09.700 --> 00:12.920
It's all thanks to you, Ivy. 
You have our gratitude.

00:12.920 --> 00:16.070
No, really! I didn't do anything!

00:16.070 --> 00:18.660
It's all because you and everyone 
else never gave up, Captain.

00:19.730 --> 00:22.960
Thank you. Now, I'd like you 
to check these, please.

00:23.420 --> 00:26.660
It's a summary of the recent events 
and a list of those arrested.

00:27.220 --> 00:29.430
There are quite a lot of people on this list.

00:29.430 --> 00:32.440
According to the report 
from the Adventurers Guild,

00:32.440 --> 00:35.270
it wasn't just the traitors 
in town who were arrested.

00:35.270 --> 00:38.980
As a result of investigations based on 
the documents obtained from their former base,

00:38.980 --> 00:41.550
fifty-eight people were added 
to a kingdom-wide wanted list

00:41.550 --> 00:45.540
and in the course of investigating, 
forty-five of them have been arrested.

00:45.540 --> 00:46.890
It wasn't just the nobility.

00:46.890 --> 00:49.560
Relatives of the royal family 
were also involved.

00:50.190 --> 00:52.570
Th-This was a really crazy organization.

00:52.570 --> 00:57.060
Yes. I had never considered that it might 
be an organization this great in size,

00:57.060 --> 00:59.290
so every time I get new 
information, I'm surprised.

00:59.290 --> 01:02.490
It really is a relief that we managed 
to resolve the situation.

01:05.240 --> 01:06.940
What is this?

01:06.940 --> 01:10.010
That's the reward which 
will be paid to you, Ivy.

01:10.010 --> 01:12.970
As compensation for your contributions 
to resolving this matter,

01:12.970 --> 01:15.000
you'll receive ten gold tablets, or 100 ladal.

01:15.000 --> 01:18.380
Since there were some wanted criminals 
among those arrested in this matter,

01:18.380 --> 01:21.820
the reward money comes 
to five gold tablets, or fifty ladal.

01:21.820 --> 01:24.020
All together, you will be paid 150 ladal.

01:24.020 --> 01:26.060
150 ladal?!

01:26.060 --> 01:30.120
Apparently, there were some really 
dangerous characters mixed up in this.

01:30.120 --> 01:32.970
Even relatives of the royal family 
with influence over the king,

01:32.970 --> 01:35.830
so the reward money you're 
receiving reflects that.

01:36.170 --> 01:38.140
<i>So, um, let's see.</i>

01:38.140 --> 01:40.210
<i>A field mouse is worth 100 dal...</i>

01:40.210 --> 01:43.360
<i>and one ladal is worth 
1,000 field mice...</i>

01:43.360 --> 01:45.810
<i>so 150 ladal would be...</i>

01:45.810 --> 01:48.360
<i>150,000 field mice worth?!</i>

01:48.360 --> 01:51.800
<i>If I add the 5,000 mice 
worth I got in Latome Village,</i>

01:51.800 --> 01:54.530
<i>that's 155,000 field mice worth!</i>

01:54.530 --> 01:56.930
If there aren't any issues, 
please sign there.

01:56.930 --> 01:58.310
Y-Yes, sir!

01:58.950 --> 02:02.350
<i>If I made dried meat from 155,000 field mice</i>

02:02.350 --> 02:06.030
<i>and ate three a day while I traveled...</i>

02:06.030 --> 02:09.690
<i>There are 365 days in a year, so...</i>

02:09.690 --> 02:11.680
<i>140 years?!</i>

02:11.680 --> 02:15.390
<i>Will I be able to live that long?</i>

02:16.330 --> 02:20.470
<i>When I'm alone, I can breathe</i>

02:20.470 --> 02:24.630
<i>In a world with no one 
but me, I feel at ease</i>

02:25.290 --> 02:29.650
<i>But I think the truth is</i>

02:29.650 --> 02:35.630
<i>That I've been waiting for 
morning's light to break through</i>

02:33.130 --> 02:41.390
<b>The Weakest Tamer
Began a Journey
to Pick Up Trash</b>

02:33.290 --> 02:35.630
<i>(Where could it be?)</i>

02:35.630 --> 02:38.880
<i>Beyond the edges of a yet unknown map</i>

02:38.880 --> 02:43.140
<i>That's where I'll find a place 
where I can live</i>

02:41.390 --> 02:43.140
<i>(If it exists...)</i>

02:43.140 --> 02:45.150
<i>I'd like to go there</i>

02:45.150 --> 02:48.900
<i>And with trembling legs, 
I take a step forward</i>

02:48.900 --> 02:51.490
<i>I'm on a journey without end</i>

02:51.490 --> 02:53.800
<i>And even if I carry nothing with me</i>

02:53.800 --> 02:55.950
<i>I'll take everything I feel</i>

02:55.950 --> 02:57.910
<i>And pack it into my once empty bag</i>

02:57.910 --> 02:59.730
<i>I'll go as far as I need to</i>

02:59.730 --> 03:01.950
<i>On this journey to find myself</i>

03:01.950 --> 03:04.040
<i>And everything I'm given along the way</i>

03:04.040 --> 03:08.500
<i>Will slowly fill my heart to the brim</i>

03:18.370 --> 03:22.730
<i>Now, I'm not all alone anymore</i>

03:22.730 --> 03:27.650
<i>Because I've met new, dear friends</i>

03:27.650 --> 03:32.400
<i>(Maybe we can understand each other 
because we're alike. Isn't it strange?)</i>

03:32.400 --> 03:35.610
<i>Your bright laughter gives me courage</i>

03:35.610 --> 03:39.870
<i>(I feel like I'm wrapped up 
snugly by your warmth)</i>

03:39.870 --> 03:45.120
<i>From now on, let's stay 
together forever and ever</i>

03:46.000 --> 03:51.000
<b>On a Journey,
the Three of Us</b>

03:59.310 --> 04:03.120
Not a single trap was 
tripped today. I wonder why.

04:04.450 --> 04:06.020
What is it, Sora?

04:07.060 --> 04:07.820
Huh?

04:10.770 --> 04:12.440
Ciel!

04:13.680 --> 04:17.210
It's been a while, Ciel! Have you been well?

04:20.070 --> 04:22.020
Huh? What is it?

04:27.570 --> 04:28.620
Ciel?

04:41.140 --> 04:43.790
Huh? "It's like having a beater 
to flush out game for a hunt"?

04:51.560 --> 04:55.270
This meat is as fresh as always, 
and it's been dressed beautifully.

04:55.270 --> 04:57.370
I'll give you 100 dal per field mouse,

04:57.370 --> 05:00.050
and today, I'll give you 100 dal 
per wild rabbit, too. What do you say?

05:00.050 --> 05:02.200
Yes, I'll take it! Thank you!

05:02.500 --> 05:05.530
All together, it comes to one gidal. 
Thanks, as always.

05:05.530 --> 05:08.340
I'm thriving thanks to you, lad.

05:08.340 --> 05:11.250
The meat is fresh and it's good 
quality, so it's very popular!

05:11.770 --> 05:13.210
Thank you!

05:13.210 --> 05:16.410
No, thank you! I'm making a lot of money here,
so you've been a huge help!

05:16.410 --> 05:19.970
After all, the meat you've brought 
in today is going right back to you, lad.

05:20.360 --> 05:21.220
What?

05:24.890 --> 05:26.760
Cheers!

05:39.240 --> 05:42.250
Now, in celebration of 
the organization's destruction...

05:42.250 --> 05:44.100
Cheers!

05:44.440 --> 05:46.450
We've rented out the whole place tonight!

05:46.450 --> 05:48.730
No standing on ceremony, all right?

05:48.730 --> 05:52.720
None of us would insist on
 observing etiquette anyway.

05:52.720 --> 05:53.920
Meat!

05:53.920 --> 05:57.180
Now, eat lots, all right, Ivy?

05:57.180 --> 05:59.500
If there's something you 
want to eat, just say so.

05:59.500 --> 06:02.020
We'll make you as much as you want!

06:02.620 --> 06:06.140
I-I have enough! I can't 
possibly eat all of this!

06:06.140 --> 06:10.670
Guys, have some sense! 
Don't push Ivy too hard.

06:10.670 --> 06:14.760
What are you talking about? You always 
 hand Ivy the biggest pile of food.

06:14.760 --> 06:18.880
Kids get bigger by eating. 
Let him eat until his belly's full.

06:18.880 --> 06:20.730
Yeah, but there's limits, you know?

06:20.730 --> 06:22.820
Thanks for all your work, Ivy.

06:23.140 --> 06:25.330
Thank you for all you've done, Mister Borolda.

06:25.330 --> 06:29.070
I heard that Count Faltoria 
finally admitted his crimes.

06:29.070 --> 06:30.160
I see.

06:30.700 --> 06:34.140
The documents we found were 
more than enough evidence,

06:34.140 --> 06:39.160
but more evidence was found in a hideout. 
That seems to have been the decisive blow.

06:39.160 --> 06:42.310
Then, all of this 
has finally come to an end.

06:42.310 --> 06:44.380
Yes, for us, at least.

06:45.070 --> 06:46.850
That Count Faltoria...

06:46.850 --> 06:50.480
I don't know if he became desperate after
being caught, but he just keeps talking.

06:50.480 --> 06:53.230
He has all sorts of stories about 
terrible things the nobility has done.

06:53.230 --> 06:54.350
Because of that,

06:54.350 --> 06:58.650
the secrets of the hidden organization causing 
trouble for the capital have been exposed,

06:58.650 --> 07:01.350
and the knights have begun 
their own investigation.

07:01.820 --> 07:05.280
I've heard that the royal capital 
is pretty hectic right now.

07:05.280 --> 07:06.750
I see.

07:06.750 --> 07:09.740
And, um, what about Green Gale?

07:09.740 --> 07:12.640
Are you worried about Meela, Ivy?

07:12.640 --> 07:13.700
Yes.

07:13.700 --> 07:17.700
Green Gale was insignificant enough 
to be used as a decoy and cast aside.

07:18.170 --> 07:20.130
They were the lowest rung on the ladder.

07:20.130 --> 07:23.650
They didn't know anything of import, 
and they haven't committed many crimes.

07:24.450 --> 07:25.930
I'm so glad.

07:26.390 --> 07:29.550
We won't have to commit any more crimes now.

07:29.550 --> 07:32.740
She betrayed the organization 
and stopped her older brothers.

07:32.740 --> 07:35.620
It seems she'll be given some lenience.

07:35.620 --> 07:36.820
I see.

07:36.820 --> 07:41.160
The GM in the royal capital sent 
both thanks and complaints my way.

07:41.160 --> 07:43.110
Thanks and complaints?

07:43.110 --> 07:48.150
Thanks for the information we sent, 
which allowed them to destroy the organization,

07:48.150 --> 07:51.580
and complaints about the sheer volume, 
which has made them all very busy.

07:51.580 --> 07:54.530
That's the situation we were in not long ago.

07:54.530 --> 07:57.520
And they're in the royal capital, 
so that makes it tougher. The poor things.

07:57.520 --> 08:00.060
That isn't the expression of a man 
who feels sorry for someone.

08:00.060 --> 08:03.920
That's because we were deserving 
of some pity, too, until very recently.

08:03.920 --> 08:07.210
The hard work we put 
in was no hardship at all.

08:07.210 --> 08:09.510
Not if it lead to 
the destruction of the organization.

08:09.510 --> 08:12.830
Right. Being busy is a trifling matter.

08:12.830 --> 08:16.390
This is all thanks to Ivy and his dear friend. 
You have our gratitude.

08:17.480 --> 08:18.730
Dear friend?

08:19.150 --> 08:20.720
I'm sorry, Ivy.

08:20.720 --> 08:23.700
We just weren't able to slip it past the GM.

08:23.700 --> 08:25.070
You mean...

08:25.070 --> 08:26.850
Yes. He knows about Sora.

08:26.850 --> 08:27.750
Oh!

08:27.750 --> 08:32.420
I'm truly sorry, Ivy. He ended 
up looking into this, you see?

08:32.820 --> 08:33.950
Oh...

08:34.420 --> 08:37.970
He looked through the records 
of every magic item in the world,

08:37.970 --> 08:40.520
and he became suspicious of this.

08:40.520 --> 08:42.990
Since it acted as the grounds 
for catching the traitors,

08:42.990 --> 08:45.630
we had to tell him the truth.

08:45.630 --> 08:48.140
Yes, I can see why you had to.

08:48.140 --> 08:50.720
I'm sorry for tricking you.

08:50.720 --> 08:53.040
There's no need to apologize, Ivy.

08:53.040 --> 08:56.290
I understand why you have to hide Sora.

08:56.290 --> 09:01.980
If anything, we're biting the hand
 that fed us. Sorry about that.

09:01.980 --> 09:04.560
Not at all! Please don't let it bother you!

09:04.560 --> 09:09.500
If it's all right with you, would you 
introduce me to your friend?

09:09.850 --> 09:11.860
Just a moment.

09:11.860 --> 09:13.580
Is it all right, Sora?

09:15.390 --> 09:18.260
This is my friend, Sora.

09:19.660 --> 09:26.180
Sora, this is Mister GM, Captain Burksby, 
and Vice-Captain Aggrop!

09:27.630 --> 09:32.190
He certainly is unusual. 
I've never seen a translucent slime before.

09:32.190 --> 09:35.000
He's rare even among 
the rarest of rare slimes!

09:35.000 --> 09:38.610
And I've never heard of one 
that could see through a lie.

09:38.610 --> 09:40.310
That's a valuable ability.

09:38.610 --> 09:40.310
He's just so adorable!

09:40.670 --> 09:41.910
Thank you, Sora.

09:41.910 --> 09:45.150
Thanks to you, peace 
has returned to this town.

09:46.770 --> 09:49.990
By the by, there's something 
I wanted to speak to Ivy about.

09:49.990 --> 09:50.990
What is it?

09:50.990 --> 09:55.490
This is only if you'd like to, but what do you 
think of continuing to live here in Otolwa?

09:55.490 --> 09:56.420
What?

09:56.420 --> 09:59.120
I heard that you're headed 
to the royal capital.

09:59.120 --> 10:02.870
But if there isn't a reason 
that you absolutely have to go,

10:02.870 --> 10:04.830
then would you consider living here?

10:06.790 --> 10:09.940
This is something we thought of, too.

10:09.940 --> 10:12.130
It doesn't have to be for forever.

10:12.130 --> 10:16.010
If there's no need to hurry on your journey, 
then won't you stay and live here a while?

10:16.010 --> 10:19.830
We'll prepare a house for you, 
along with anything else you might need.

10:19.830 --> 10:23.730
You saved our town. 
At least let us do this much for you.

10:23.730 --> 10:26.790
This town is going to become 
an even better place to live.

10:26.790 --> 10:28.190
We'd all welcome you.

10:28.190 --> 10:30.240
What do you think, Ivy?

10:30.240 --> 10:33.150
Will you live with all of us 
here in this town?

10:34.320 --> 10:36.500
With all of you?

10:45.470 --> 10:50.630
One day, you must take a journey to see 
the world and broaden your perspective.

10:50.630 --> 10:54.720
When you do, go to the town 
neighboring the royal capital.

10:55.080 --> 10:59.640
But if you find a place where you'd like 
to live forever while on your journey,

10:59.640 --> 11:01.890
there's no need to force yourself 
to keep traveling.

11:01.890 --> 11:05.310
However, you must find 
people that you can trust.

11:05.870 --> 11:09.000
<i>When you do, you must tell them everything.</i>

11:11.790 --> 11:15.150
There's something I have to tell all of you.

11:18.050 --> 11:19.140
The truth is...

11:19.750 --> 11:21.430
The truth is I...

11:22.780 --> 11:24.080
I'm starless.

11:26.020 --> 11:30.200
I have a zero-star tamer skill.

11:31.840 --> 11:36.660
When I was five, my skill 
was checked at a church.

11:37.090 --> 11:41.220
I was a tamer. But I was starless.

11:41.950 --> 11:44.750
I was told that the gods had abandoned me.

11:44.750 --> 11:47.270
After that, everything changed.

11:47.570 --> 11:51.910
My parents and everyone 
around me became my enemies.

11:52.730 --> 11:57.340
Everyone except for one person, 
a fortune teller who saved me.

11:58.490 --> 12:04.180
When I was eight, they said a starless
 would bring misfortune to the village.

12:04.560 --> 12:07.950
I was nearly killed
 and ran away from the village.

12:08.960 --> 12:12.170
Back then, I was so sad and so frustrated...

12:12.170 --> 12:14.090
I just wanted to live, so I ran.

12:14.790 --> 12:17.800
I was scared because I didn't know 
how long I'd have to run...

12:18.510 --> 12:20.540
and I didn't know where to run to.

12:22.150 --> 12:23.380
And so...

12:24.190 --> 12:27.750
And so I kept running... all the way here.

12:31.820 --> 12:35.200
That's... who I am.

12:42.030 --> 12:44.530
I see. Well done persevering this far!

12:47.040 --> 12:49.610
It must have been so hard all this time.

12:50.040 --> 12:55.080
I feel so badly for you. I'm amazed that you 
didn't lose heart under those circumstances.

12:55.080 --> 12:56.760
You're so strong, Ivy.

12:56.760 --> 12:59.320
You never have to feel that way again.

12:59.320 --> 13:01.940
Yes, because we're here for you, all right?

13:07.520 --> 13:10.710
You don't ever have to worry 
about your stars again.

13:10.710 --> 13:14.850
If you don't want people to know, 
we'll keep it a secret amongst ourselves.

13:14.850 --> 13:15.700
Right?

13:15.700 --> 13:16.400
Of course!

13:16.900 --> 13:19.900
We swear that no one here will 
speak of it to anyone else.

13:19.900 --> 13:21.240
You can rest easy about that.

13:23.580 --> 13:26.420
Thank you so much, everyone!

13:26.920 --> 13:27.840
Now, I...

13:28.730 --> 13:31.300
Now, I can leave on my journey 
with my heart at ease!

13:32.330 --> 13:35.090
But why?! Aren't you going to live here?

13:36.850 --> 13:40.530
Up until now, my journey 
has been about running away.

13:40.530 --> 13:44.280
I thought that if people found out 
I was starless, I'd be killed.

13:44.660 --> 13:50.190
But then I met Captain Oggto 
and Vice-Captain Vellivera in Latome.

13:50.190 --> 13:53.190
They must have known that unusual 
circumstances had brought me there,

13:53.190 --> 13:56.220
but they didn't ask me anything. 
They just helped me.

13:56.560 --> 13:59.020
They even served as my guarantors.

13:59.860 --> 14:04.700
And all of you, too! When you found out 
I was being targeted, you helped me.

14:04.700 --> 14:07.640
You even went along with my reckless plan.

14:09.250 --> 14:13.210
All of you are different 
from the people I knew.

14:13.210 --> 14:16.230
The fortune teller told me 
to go learn more about the world.

14:16.230 --> 14:19.890
I finally understand what 
she really meant by that!

14:20.950 --> 14:25.010
And thanks to all of you, I've changed.

14:25.410 --> 14:26.960
I won't run anymore.

14:27.970 --> 14:31.500
I'm perfectly fine as a starless!

14:32.610 --> 14:33.720
Ivy...

14:34.190 --> 14:39.330
From now on, my journey won't be 
about running away, but about finding things.

14:39.330 --> 14:40.630
Finding things?

14:40.630 --> 14:44.040
Yes! I want to find something 
that I want to do.

14:44.040 --> 14:47.780
Something that I can do for others 
even though I have nothing right now.

14:47.780 --> 14:49.560
Well said, Ivy!

14:49.560 --> 14:52.500
Yes! If that's what you want, 
then seeing the world is the best thing to do!

14:52.500 --> 14:57.540
There are adventurers who have opened up inns, 
and others who have opened up taverns.

14:57.540 --> 14:59.960
It's possible to become 
whatever you want to.

14:59.960 --> 15:03.550
Yes! And of course, there are some 
who have opened up sweets shops, too!

15:03.970 --> 15:05.010
Right!

15:05.010 --> 15:07.550
Well, then. You're really going, huh?

15:07.550 --> 15:11.260
And just when we'd gotten to know you.
Makes it harder to say goodbye.

15:11.260 --> 15:13.700
Yes, for me, too.

15:13.700 --> 15:15.440
Little Sora, are you going, too?

15:15.440 --> 15:17.530
I'll be so lonely!

15:18.320 --> 15:21.860
All right. Since that's the case, 
tonight, we drink!

15:21.860 --> 15:26.320
Yeah! Everyone, enjoy yourselves 
while Ivy's still in town!

15:26.320 --> 15:28.320
Yeah!

15:46.070 --> 15:47.780
Go! Go! Go!

15:47.780 --> 15:49.130
You know...

15:54.770 --> 15:56.560
Huh? It's nothing.

15:57.770 --> 16:01.270
This is what they call "happiness," right?

16:14.130 --> 16:15.040
All right.

16:15.820 --> 16:18.500
You haven't forgotten anything? 
Do you have the lunch we packed?

16:18.500 --> 16:21.290
What about water? Did you check your tent?

16:21.290 --> 16:23.170
Should I carry the heavier stuff for you?

16:24.380 --> 16:25.970
That's enough of that.

16:25.970 --> 16:28.100
He's a lot more dependable than you are.

16:28.100 --> 16:29.340
Right, Ivy?

16:29.800 --> 16:33.330
Yes, I have everything I'll need in these.

16:33.330 --> 16:35.610
I'll be all right, Mister Lattrua!

16:36.010 --> 16:39.520
Really? Well, if you say so.

16:40.030 --> 16:43.410
Thanks to the official magic 
bags you've all given me,

16:43.410 --> 16:45.920
it's so much easier 
to carry all of my things!

16:45.920 --> 16:49.960
The official ones carry much more, 
and they weigh a lot less.

16:49.960 --> 16:52.200
They also have the ability to stop time,

16:52.200 --> 16:54.360
so if you put food in them, 
the food won't rot.

16:54.360 --> 16:55.880
They're essential for any journey.

16:55.880 --> 16:57.950
Thank you all so very much!

16:57.950 --> 17:01.170
They're items that drop all the time 
when you defeat monsters.

17:01.460 --> 17:03.160
Don't worry and just take them with you.

17:03.160 --> 17:04.110
I will!

17:05.010 --> 17:06.400
Sora, you take care, too!

17:06.400 --> 17:08.300
See you later, dear Sora!

17:08.720 --> 17:13.090
Speaking of which, I looked into 
disintegrating slimes after that conversation.

17:13.090 --> 17:14.120
What?

17:14.120 --> 17:18.800
There wasn't much information, but as 
disintegrating slimes are incredibly weak,

17:18.800 --> 17:24.070
even a one-star tamer's magic is too strong
for them, and they die during taming.

17:24.070 --> 17:25.590
I didn't know that.

17:25.590 --> 17:29.190
I've heard that starless 
lack power in all aspects.

17:29.570 --> 17:34.100
Which means that perhaps Sora was only able 
to be tamed because it was you who did it, Ivy.

17:34.910 --> 17:41.040
And if you hadn't tamed him, he may have 
disintegrated and disappeared just like that.

17:43.730 --> 17:47.900
<i>What? "Maybe Sora existed just to meet me"?</i>

17:47.900 --> 17:53.540
Yes. And that means that I came 
into existence to meet Sora, too.

17:57.560 --> 17:58.640
Yes!

18:01.250 --> 18:03.340
Look after yourself, Ivy.

18:03.340 --> 18:06.530
If you change your mind, 
you can come back any time.

18:06.530 --> 18:08.470
And you can come back just to see us, too.

18:08.470 --> 18:10.860
Please think of this town as your home.

18:11.210 --> 18:12.870
Thank you!

18:15.010 --> 18:17.580
Well then, everyone! Take care!

18:17.580 --> 18:20.710
Take care, Ivy!

18:18.570 --> 18:20.710
Bye, Ivy! Take care!

18:20.710 --> 18:22.290
We'll see each other again!

18:22.290 --> 18:26.040
Ivy! Safe travels! Ivy! Ivy!

18:39.130 --> 18:41.640
Is that... an adandala?

18:41.640 --> 18:43.310
Don't tell me that it's also...

18:43.700 --> 18:45.740
A starless tamer, huh?

18:45.740 --> 18:49.270
Compared to people who have stars and don't 
use them well, he seems a lot more powerful.

18:54.860 --> 18:58.600
<i>What? "It's sad leaving everyone behind"?</i>

18:58.980 --> 19:02.450
Yes, it's sad, but...

19:04.800 --> 19:06.040
Ciel!

19:23.860 --> 19:25.860
<i>My name is Ivy.</i>

19:26.170 --> 19:28.000
<i>I have a tamer skill.</i>

19:28.000 --> 19:32.580
<i>I have no stars... 
but I have a </i>lot<i> of friends!</i>

19:35.020 --> 19:38.610
<i>You are not alone</i>

19:38.610 --> 19:42.170
<i>Open your eyes</i>

19:42.170 --> 19:43.960
<i>That’s the way</i>

19:43.960 --> 19:48.660
<i>You’ll be fine</i>

19:48.660 --> 19:52.740
<i>All of us are here now</i>

19:52.740 --> 19:58.560
<i>You’re something special</i>

19:58.560 --> 20:05.830
<i>Please just relax, and move forward</i>

20:06.820 --> 20:11.240
<i>Because you are here now</i>

20:11.240 --> 20:16.100
<i>The world is so beautiful</i>

20:16.100 --> 20:21.850
<i>This place is full of light</i>

20:21.850 --> 20:28.470
<i>You had countless nights of tears</i>

20:28.470 --> 20:35.860
<i>But you walked all the way here</i>

20:35.860 --> 20:42.180
<i>If it’s dark we’ll be your light</i>

20:42.180 --> 20:52.010
<i>You see the end of this road 
is crystal clear</i>
